{"abstract":[{"text":"What the ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" types do that their signatures do not say.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/synapsessdk\/workingwithmodels"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SynapsesSDK"}],"role":"article","title":"Working with the models","roleHeading":"Article"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/GettingStarted","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/Positioning","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/Maps","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/LiveData","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/BlueGPS","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/APIError","doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/EnvironmentModel"],"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Most model types in this SDK are plain data: they mirror the JSON the backend sends, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reading the properties is enough to know what you get. A handful of behaviours, though,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are not visible in the declarations and will bite if you assume otherwise. They are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"listed here once rather than repeated on every type.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"Default values do not survive decoding","type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Default-values-do-not-survive-decoding"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A property written like this looks like it defaults to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public var required: Bool? = false"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"It does — but only when you construct the value in Swift. The synthesized ","type":"text"},{"code":"Decodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"uses ","type":"text"},{"code":"decodeIfPresent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", so when the key is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"absent from the JSON the property decodes to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":", not to the default"}]},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"false"},{"type":"text","text":" are then two different states you have to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tell apart yourself."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Treat every ","type":"text"},{"code":"T? = someDefault","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in a decoded model as “may be ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whatever the default","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"suggests”, and write the fallback at the point of use:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["if element.required ?? false { … }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The properties this applies to carry a note saying so."}]},{"text":"`id` is local, not the backend’s identifier","anchor":"id-is-local-not-the-backends-identifier","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Several models are "},{"code":"Identifiable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" through a property declared like this:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["public var id = UUID()"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"That property is ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"not","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" in the type’s "},{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so it is never decoded: a fresh UUID"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is minted every time an instance is created, decoding included. Two decodes of the very"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same JSON therefore carry different "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This matters more than it looks, because "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" include ","type":"text"},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":":","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"comparing two instances decoded from identical payloads returns "},{"code":"false","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and they land in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different buckets of a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or a dictionary. Use it as SwiftUI identity within one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"render pass — that is what it is for — and compare backend identity through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"backend’s own field (","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/commentId","type":"reference"},{"text":", a resource’s own id, and so on).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Watch for the related remap: in "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" the JSON field "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"text":" decodes into","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/commentId","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", precisely because "},{"code":"id","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is taken."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Timestamps are milliseconds","anchor":"Timestamps-are-milliseconds","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Backend timestamps arrive as ","type":"text"},{"code":"Double","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"milliseconds"}]},{"type":"text","text":" since the epoch, not seconds —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/BGPGPSPosition\/positionTS"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/creationTimestamp","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and their siblings.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Passing one straight to ","type":"text"},{"code":"Date(timeIntervalSince1970:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" gives a date tens of thousands of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"years in the future. Divide by 1000, or use the convenience the model already offers","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/TicketComment\/creationDate","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The exceptions announce themselves in the name: fields ending in ","type":"text"},{"code":"Second","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.synapseslab.BlueGPS.SynapsesSDK\/documentation\/SynapsesSDK\/BGPSPositionCoordinator\/lastPositionNotOlderThan(_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whose "},{"code":"seconds","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" parameter is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fact compared against a millisecond difference.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"Unknown-enum-values-decode-they-do-not-throw","type":"heading","text":"Unknown enum values decode, they do not throw"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Enums conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SafeCodableEnums"},{"type":"text","text":" map any value this SDK version does not recognise"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"onto their last case — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UNKNOWN"},{"type":"text","text":", or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"unknown"},{"type":"text","text":". A backend that adds a new status will not"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"break decoding, so a ","type":"text"},{"code":"switch","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over one of these enums must handle that case rather than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"assume the set is closed. Never send ","type":"text"},{"code":"UNKNOWN","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" back: it is an inbound fallback, not a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"value the backend accepts.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some collections offer a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"filterUnknownValues"},{"type":"text","text":" flag to drop those entries instead of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handing them to you."}]},{"anchor":"Memberwise-initialisers-are-internal","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Memberwise initialisers are internal"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Model structs get the compiler’s memberwise initialiser, and it is "},{"code":"internal","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — so fro